  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supplementary support for Kambia District Ebola Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to support the District Ebola Response, in Sierra Leone.
Catholic relief Services (CRS) Sierra Leone has secured funding from United Nations Mission for Ebola Emergency Response (UNMEER) for the SMART Alliance partnership to support the District Ebola Response, with the primary aim of stopping the outbreak and preventing the spread of the Ebola virus. 
With Kambia remaining as a key district, and a recent ramping up of efforts to stop the spread of the Ebola virus with the UNMEER backed Kambia Community Action plan, this funding will support the DERC and CAFOD to continue and strengthen operations. 

There are two components of funding which have been informed by key requests from the District Ebola Response Center (DERC). 

1. On-going goods and services for the Command and Control Center. 
2. Support to the Kambia Community Action Plan (KCAP)</narrative>
  </description>
